Published: `@claude-flow/cli`, `claude-flow` and `ruflo` 3.78.0 on `latest`. The `@claude-flow/mcp` 3.1.8 and `@claude-flow/security` 3.0.8 standalone packages were also republished.

It is a minor bump because `@claude-flow/neural` 3.1.0 and `@claude-flow/memory` 3.4.0 (#5041) add surface.

## Since 3.77.2
- Security:
  - #5032: authenticate `/ws` upgrades and compare tokens in constant time (`@claude-flow/shared` 3.0.10);
  - #4962: transport and WebSocket limits;
  - #5021: zod 4 migration;
  - #5039: guard every `.claude-flow` write and sign the companion helpers (integrates #4991);
  - #5037: show learned lessons only from a file this machine wrote (integrates #4854);
  - #3835: settings.json risk scanner on session-restore.
- Dream cycle:
  - #5041: neural/memory fixes (integrates #4660, #4973, #4081, #3650, #4983, #5034, #5012);
  - #5004: `guidance_brain` coverage;
  - #4989: swarm consensus listener limits. `@claude-flow/swarm` is not republished, so this stays inert in the installed CLI.
- Other:
  - #4822: memory lock ownership;
  - #4641: chat-ui;
  - #4995: `init --dry-run`;
  - #5040: MCP tool coverage (integrates #4840).

## Leaf packages
- `mcp` 3.1.7 → 3.1.8 and `security` 3.0.7 → 3.0.8. These are bundled, so the train already carries their source. The bump is so the standalone packages pick up #4962 and #5021, which landed after the Nov 9 publishes. Both get a standalone publish after merge.
- The non-bundled leaves (`shared` 3.0.10, `neural` 3.1.0, `memory` 3.4.0) were published before their pins merged.


Install: `npx ruflo@latest`

# Features

## Deferred decoding with `deferDecoding`

`Rive` and `RiveFile` now take a `deferDecoding` option. When it is on, parts of a `.riv` are decoded the first time they are used instead of when the file loads. Animations decode the first time they play, artboards other than the default one decode the first time they are instanced, and view model instances decode the first time they are handed out. Large files with many artboards, animations, or view model instances load faster when a page uses only some of them. ([Change](https://github.com/rive-app/rive-wasm/commit/ab52f71a3585560da8ca28a2ae49622180f894b1))

It is off by default. On a `Rive` instance, the flag applies only when that instance loads its own file (`src` or `buffer`). If you pass a `riveFile`, the file's own setting is used instead.

```ts
const r = new Rive({
  src: "large.riv",
  canvas,
  deferDecoding: true,
});
```

## Per-text language for shaping and font fallback

Text, text runs, and text inputs can now have a language set in the Editor, similar to HTML's lang. Fonts use the language to pick their localized glyph forms. The fallback font callback now also receives the languages as a third argument, so you can choose, for example, a Japanese font over a Chinese font for the same Han character. Text with no language of its own follows navigator.languages and updates when the browser's languages change. (Change (https://github.com/rive-app/rive-wasm/commit/48e82a16056219d75d4f0db80f4141184c9d95a5))

To override the browser's languages:
```
RiveFont.setSystemLanguages(["ja-JP", "en-US"]);
RiveFont.setFallbackFontsCallback((missingGlyph, weight, languages) => {
  return languages[0]?.startsWith("ja") ? japaneseFont : defaultFont;
});
```

